---
description: Avoid token-heavy supervision of long-running automated tasks
alwaysApply: true
---

# Long-running task monitoring

- After starting a long-running local or remote automated command, do not continuously poll or narrate unchanged status.
- Let the process run independently. Prefer a single delayed completion check, a background job, CI notification, or a saved log/result file.
- Check again only near the expected completion time, when the task reports completion, or when user action is required.
- Do not spend model turns merely waiting. Use the resulting logs and structured reports to diagnose failures after the run finishes.
- For long local builds and test suites, tell the user that the task has started and yield control unless active interaction is genuinely required.
